<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johan Ferrier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/2010">2010</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johan Ferrier was a Surinamese teacher and politician who served as prime minister from 1955 to 1958, as governor of the autonomous country of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> from 1968 and as the first president of the independent republic from 1975. He was removed from office in 1980, months after the military coup of that year, and spent most of his later life in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, where he died aged 99.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johan-ferrier.jpg" alt="Johan Ferrier" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bert Verhoeff for Anefo; , Nationaal Archief, Den Haag, Rijksfotoarchief: Fotocollectie Algemeen Nederlands Fotopersbureau … · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferrier_in_Suriname_1975_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
